course: dictionary
lesson: 1212
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as 1) and 2). To choose the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «A pet budgie is a flock bird living in a house.» The clues are pet and house, so here a budgie is the small bird kept in a cage.
explain: Now read this: «In Australia, a wild budgerigar lives in big flocks in the dry inland.» The clues are wild and Australia, so budgie can also mean a bird living freely outside, not a pet.
explain: Context can also tell you how a bird is feeling. «Head-bobbing usually means a budgie is excited or showing off.» Head-bobbing is a clue to the bird's mood. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence, and does my meaning still make sense when I put it in?
fact: A budgie is a small, bright parrot, and its full name is budgerigar.
fact: Budgies are often green, blue or yellow.
fact: In the USA, a budgie is often called a parakeet.
fact: «Budgies are very chatty birds that chatter and whistle a lot.» Chatty means talking a lot.
fact: Budgies are flock birds, so a budgie is happiest with another budgie beside it.
exercise: «A pet budgie is a flock bird living in a house.» What does budgie mean here? | *A small parrot kept as a pet | A kind of cage | A wild bird living in the dry inland | A flock of birds in the sky
exercise: «Wild budgies live in big flocks in the dry inland of Australia.» Which meaning is used here? | A toy for a bird | A small bird kept in a house | A type of cage for birds | *A wild budgerigar living freely in flocks
exercise: «Head-bobbing usually means a budgie is excited or showing off.» What does head-bobbing usually mean? | *The budgie is excited or showing off | The budgie is asleep | The budgie is living in the wild | The budgie needs a bigger cage
test: «Budgies are very chatty birds.» What does chatty mean? | Angry and grumpy | *Talking and chattering a lot | Blue all over | Quiet and still
test: Jayden says, «A budgie is always a pet.» Is he right? | *No, wild budgies live in flocks in Australia | Yes, all birds are pets | No, a budgie is a kind of fish | Yes, budgies only live in cages
exam: Which clue tells you which meaning of budgie to use? | The name of the bird's owner | The number of letters in the word | The colour of the cage | *The words around it, like pet or wild
